title: CrowdStrike FalconFlank Privilege Escalation via Macro Remediation
id: c8d4e9f2-5a3b-48c7-b6d9-2e0f8a3c1d57
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects potential exploitation of the FalconFlank zero-day vulnerability in
    CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor for Windows. The exploit abuses Falcon's Office
    malicious macros remediation feature to escalate to SYSTEM privileges. This
    rule detects the anomalous pattern of Falcon's remediation process spawning
    shell interpreters (cmd.exe, powershell.exe) with elevated privileges, which
    indicates the remediation workflow is being abused for privilege escalation.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com
    - https://cyberpress.org
    - https://github.com/MSNightmare/FalconFlank
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/05
tags:
    - attack.t1068
    - attack.t1548
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_falcon_shell:
        ParentImage|endswith:
            - '\falconsvc.exe'
            - '\falconcontainer.exe'
            - '\CSFalconService.exe'
        Image|endswith:
            - '\cmd.exe'
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
            - '\conhost.exe'
    selection_falcon_spawn:
        Image|endswith: '\falconsvc.exe'
        IntegrityLevel: 'System'
    condition: selection_falcon_shell or selection_falcon_spawn
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate Falcon remediation actions (rare, should be validated with CrowdStrike support)
    - Falcon service process spawning conhost.exe for logging output (uncommon)
level: high
